  "evaluation_scope": [
    "The holdout removes later exact-text occurrences from ten saved lyric records, resets all timings, and processes complete original audio.",
    "Correctness is checked against supplied text and earlier saved CTC timings, not independently human-annotated ground truth.",
    "Matching uses normalized text and start-time difference below 0.5 seconds. If an old saved word stretches over a music break, at least 80% of comparable word boundaries must agree instead. This rule is applied uniformly.",
    "The first and second production API results both pass word binding, finite in-range timing and preserved-row checks.",
    "This establishes 153/153 recovery under this test protocol; it is not a universal zero-error or human-audited timing guarantee.",
    "Low-confidence flags remain. No automatic manual approval is performed.",
    "An independent Whisper probe on three short difficult excerpts returned unrelated subtitle phrases; it was inconclusive and was not treated as evidence of correctness.",
    "Original recordings and saved user lyrics are not overwritten by the test runner."
  ],
